{
  "analysis": "The ELF is a 32-bit little-endian MIPS executable (MIPSEL), entry 0x400090, with 5 program headers. The Makefile shows it was compiled with clang to MIPS32R2 little-endian static, using a custom my_stdlib and no libc. We need to inspect the custom stdlib/syscall stubs and image saving code to know what syscalls and rendering hooks the interpreter must support.",
  "plan": "Inspect program headers and key source files: my_stdlib.c/h, doomgeneric_img.c, doomgeneric.h, i_video.c, and any syscall references. This will reveal the ABI/syscalls and how frames are saved.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport struct\nb=open('doomgeneric_mips','rb').read()\nphoff=52; phentsize=32; phnum=5\nfor i in range(phnum):\n    off=phoff+i*phentsize\n    p=b[off:off+phentsize]\n    typ,off2,vaddr,paddr,filesz,memsz,flags,align=struct.unpack('<IIIIIIII',p)\n    print(i, 'type',typ,'offset',off2,'vaddr',hex(vaddr),'filesz',filesz,'memsz',memsz,'flags',flags,'align',align)\nPY\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,260p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.h\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,320p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,260p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,220p' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric.h\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -R \"syscall\\\\|DG_Init\\\\|DG_DrawFrame\\\\|DoomMain\\\\|frame\" -n doomgeneric/doomgeneric | head -100\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
